WEBVTT

00:00:01.330 --> 00:00:06.920
Qwen3.8-27B at 450 tokens a second: what the number counts.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:10.834
Batch size one, and a speculative-decoding number.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.835
Tokens per second at 8K, same model and card.

00:00:16.835 --> 00:00:20.192
Speculation off, 71.2; the headline, 450.78.

00:00:20.192 --> 00:00:21.870
That is 6.33×.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:26.905
The off figure is a retained upstream NInfer run.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.847
Why the long-context figure holds up.

00:00:30.847 --> 00:00:35.042
48 of 64: layers with no growing KV cache.

00:00:35.042 --> 00:00:36.441
Architecture, not engineering.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:43.779
106.72 s of prefill for the 260,000-token request.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.136
A strong per-user result, and a statement about the workload.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:55.358
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
